      "title": "Avatar Generation - Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## One connected avatar workflow\n\nSet ModelArk, Seed Speech and Vision AI keys in **Settings > BytePlus**. Sign in to Comfy.org for connected-media uploads.\n\nEdit the character prompt and spoken words, then Run once. Seedream and Seed Audio feed OmniHuman directly: **no review pause** and no separate app.\n\nThe optional upload nodes are muted and disconnected. Unmute the loader you want to use and upload a file. For a character reference, connect Load Image to Seedream's image_1. To replace a generated input, connect Load Image or Load Audio directly to OmniHuman, then mute the unused generator AND its save node to avoid extra generation.\n\nKeep generation_count at 1. Narration must be 4-300 seconds for OmniHuman; start with a short spoken script. Outputs save under BytePlus/Avatar.\n\nSeed controls stay fixed to allow cached inputs to be reused. Change a seed for a fresh take; changed inputs, a cleared cache or a restart can generate and bill again.\n\nFor an unresolved video, keep its inputs and seed unchanged. Use existing_task_id on OmniHuman to recover the original task; do not generate a replacement blindly. To avoid upstream generation during recovery, disconnect image/audio from OmniHuman and mute their generators and savers first. Task Result is also available as a separate node."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## One connected avatar workflow\n\nSet ModelArk, Seed Speech and Vision AI keys in **Settings > BytePlus**. Sign in to Comfy.org for connected-media uploads.\n\nEdit the character prompt and spoken words, then Run once. Seedream and Seed Audio feed OmniHuman directly: **no review pause** and no separate app.\n\nThe optional upload nodes are muted and disconnected. Unmute the loader you want to use and upload a file. For a character reference, connect Load Image to Seedream's image_1. To replace a generated input, connect Load Image or Load Audio directly to OmniHuman, then mute the unused generator AND its save node to avoid extra generation.\n\nKeep generation_count at 1. Narration must be 4-300 seconds for OmniHuman; start with a short spoken script. Outputs save under BytePlus/Avatar.\n\nSeed controls stay fixed to allow cached inputs to be reused. Change a seed for a fresh take; changed inputs, a cleared cache or a restart can generate and bill again.\n\nFor an unresolved video, keep its inputs and seed unchanged. Use existing_task_id on OmniHuman to recover the original task; do not generate a replacement blindly. To avoid upstream generation during recovery, disconnect image/audio from OmniHuman and mute their generators and savers first. Task Result is also available as a separate node."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
